# decision Nix flake inputs carry ref, rev, and dir in a native Git URL

The Nix adapter owns one delimited `inputs.<name>.url` assignment in `flake.nix`. Wiring uses a
`git+` URL with both the declared `ref` and `LockedDependency.Commit` as `rev`. An export
subdirectory becomes the native `dir` query parameter. Query encoding is deterministic. `Pull`
updates exactly the selected input in `flake.lock`; the declaration edit by itself does not claim
success.

# test Nix adapter

- Fixture/golden wiring is idempotent and preserves unrelated Nix expressions and comments.
- Drift checks the normalized Git URL and locked `rev`.
- Unwire removes only the delimited input assignment.
- The central native-lifecycle runner uses pinned Nix 2.28.3 and the public CLI to prove real
  evaluation, read-only list, fresh-clone and missing-lock repair, targeted advance, rollback,
  and removal while preserving an unrelated flake input.

# decision flake materialization

`Pull` requires `nix` before mutation and runs `nix flake lock --update-input <name>` on every
call, including an unchanged commit, so a missing lock node is repaired and fetched. `Remove`
deletes the owned input then runs `nix flake lock` to prune it. `Inspect` verifies the exact locked
revision without invoking Nix.
